 where e+f = 0 or 1, with e = 0 or 1 and f = 0 or 1 in which formulae, symbol 45 \f "Symbol" \s 10- the R1 symbols, which are identical or different, represent a saturated or unsaturated, linear or branched, aliphatic radical containing from 1 to 10 carbon atoms or a phenyl radical, optionally substituted by fluoro or cyano groups; symbol 45 \f "Symbol" \s 10- the A symbols, which are identical or different, represent a primary, secondary, tertiary or quatemized amino group bonded to the silicon via an SiC bond; 

 symbol 45 \f "Symbol" \s 10- the B symbols, which are identical or different, represent symbol 45 \f "Symbol" \s 10- an OH functional group; symbol 45 \f "Symbol" \s 10- an OR functional group, where R represents an alkyl group containing from 1 to 12 carbon atoms, preferably from 3 to 6 carbon atoms, very particularly 4 carbon atoms; symbol 45 \f "Symbol" \s 10- an OCOR' functional group, where R' represents an alkyl group containing from 1 to 12 carbon atoms, preferably 1 carbon atom; or symbol 45 \f "Symbol" \s 10- the A symbol.
